    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d291">

                <pb facs="0456" n="368" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg368"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 772.73/7</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to King Nicholas I of Montenegro</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-01-09">9 January,
                            1919</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Good Friend</hi>: I have received your letter of
                    January seventh and read it with considerable interest. I must at present
                    content myself with a brief acknowledgment of it, but I beg that you will
                    believe that the days will not be too crowded or too hurried for me to drive the
                    interests of sturdy Montenegro out of my mind or to lessen in the least my
                    sincere desire to do everything in my power to see that justice is done her. The
                    matters to which you call my attention will have my most serious and sympathetic
                    consideration.</p>
                <p>Cordially and faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodrow Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
